  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 605.01 Immediate Notice of Certain Hazardous Materials Incidents.\n\n(a) Each motor carrier who transports hazardous materials shall immediately notify the department after any incident pursuant to 49 CFR 171.15 which has occurred during the course of transportation, loading, unloading, or storage.\n\n(b) Each notification pursuant to (a) above shall be given to the department by telephone at state police headquarters, (603) 223-4381. Interstate shippers shall give notice to federal agencies pursuant to the requirements of 49 CFR 171.15.\n\n(c) Each notification pursuant to (a) above shall include the following:\n\n(1) The reporting party’s name;\n\n(2) The name and address of reporting party’s motor carrier;\n\n(3) The telephone number where reporting party can be contacted;\n\n(4) The date, time, and location of incident;\n\n(5) The extent of injuries, if any;\n\n(6) The classification, name, and quantity of hazardous materials involved, if available; and\n\n(7) The type of incident, nature of hazardous materials involved, and whether a continuing danger to life exists at the scene.\n\n(d) Each motor carrier who makes a report pursuant to this section shall also make the report required by Saf-C 605.02.\n\nSource. #1461 eff. 10-16-79; ss by #2249, eff 12-31-82; ss by #2945, eff 1-3-85, EXPIRED: 1-3-91\n\nNew. #5219, eff 9-4-91; ss by #6562, Interim, eff 9-4-97, EXPIRES: 1-2-98\n\nNew. #8721-B, eff 9-8-06, EXPIRED: 9-8-14\n\nNew. #12373, INTERIM, eff 8-31-17, EXPIRED: 2-27-18\n\nNew. #12516, eff 4-23-18",
